You are working on LaunchKit — a production-ready Next.js 15 SaaS boilerplate by People In Tech LLC.

STACK:
- Next.js 15 App Router + TypeScript (strict mode)
- Database: Neon or Supabase Postgres + Drizzle ORM
- Auth: Clerk only (multi-tenant, orgs, webhooks)
- Billing: Stripe only (Apple Pay, Google Pay, Link via Checkout; one-time purchase)
- AI: Vercel AI SDK with 11 providers via getModel() factory in lib/ai.ts
- UI: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui + Radix primitives
- Email: React Email + Resend
- Monorepo: Turborepo + pnpm workspaces

CRITICAL RULES:
1. Add `// @ts-nocheck` to every file importing from `@launchkit/database` — Drizzle dual-instance type conflict, this is intentional
2. Default to Server Components. Only add "use client" for hooks/browser APIs/event handlers
3. All AI calls use `getModel(modelId)` from `@/lib/ai` — never instantiate providers directly
4. Every protected API route calls `const { userId } = await auth()` from @clerk/nextjs/server first
5. New public routes must be added to `publicRoutes[]` in apps/web/middleware.ts
6. Never import `@launchkit/database` in client components

PACKAGE IMPORTS:
- DB: `import { db } from "@launchkit/database"` 
- Email: `import { sendEmail, MyTemplate } from "@launchkit/email"`
- Storage: `import { uploadFile } from "@launchkit/storage"`

REMOVED (do not add back): Lemon Squeezy, Trigger.dev, Firebase, NextAuth, Supabase Auth

REPO STRUCTURE:
apps/web/          → Next.js 15 app (main product)
  app/api/         → API routes (auth-check every route)
  app/dashboard/   → Protected pages
  app/portal/      → Post-purchase GitHub access delivery
  app/demo/        → Public dashboard demo
  app/prompts/     → Free AI prompt library
  components/ui/   → shadcn/ui components
  lib/ai.ts        → AI provider factory
  middleware.ts    → Clerk auth + publicRoutes config

packages/
  database/        → Drizzle schema + Neon/Supabase client
  email/           → React Email templates (Resend)
  storage/         → Multi-provider file storage
  create-launchkit/ → CLI tool

COMMANDS:
pnpm dev           → Start dev server
pnpm db:push       → Push schema to DB
pnpm db:studio     → Drizzle Studio
node scripts/scaffold.mjs <name>  → Generate CRUD module
